  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e8e4fafc6c03f7a49b6d2a8b3143e463, type: 3}
  m_Name: Territorial Conflict
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::EventInfo
  eventName: Territorial Conflict
  eventDescription: As your team is navigating the terrain they come to a sudden
    stop. Before you have a chance to ask why they point further ahead where the
    local species, the insectoids and fungi, are in the middle of a conflict. You
    would walk away, but you could also influcence the conflict to come...
  eventOptions:
  - '[Fight] Order your team to intervene on behalf of of the insectoids. Better
    to deal with insectoids than hordes of fungi. '
  - '[Fight] Command the team to attack the insectoids. Their adapations are an equal
    threat to you and the insectoids.'
  - Let them kill one another, you don't have time to pick fights that don't involve
    you.
  eventResults:
  - 'As the last fungi falls you order your squad to keep their weapons up, but quickly
    find the order to be unnecessary. The insectoids simply walk by, making no efforts
    to continue the violence. In their wake you find a piece of broken carapace,
    proof of your deeds today.


    The party obtains an Insectoid Carapace talisman. '
  - 'When the dust settles your team is surrounded by insectoids. You grit your teeth,
    expecting you act of kindness to not go unpunished. Instead, the fungi present
    a you with a flask containing a strange liquid. The moment you take it the creatures
    disappear. If this is their thank you, you''re certain it will be short lived.


    The
    party obtains a Fungal Brew consumable. '
  - Your team lays low skulks away, what surely would have been a blood conflict.
